OL,3,ANvidia-backed data centre firm scraps
OL,4,AIPO as AI valuation concerns deepen
OL,5,
OL,6,FArtificial intelligence (AI) data
OL,7,Fcentre company Firmus has scrapped its
OL,8,Fplans for what would have been one of
OL,9,FAustralia's biggest-ever stock market
OL,10,Flistings.
OL,12,FThe Nvidia-backed firm said it had made
OL,13,Fthe decision due to "recent market
OL,14,Fvolatility and prevailing market
OL,15,Fconditions" and that going public would
OL,16,Fnot be in the company or shareholders'
OL,17,Fbest interests.
OL,19,FFirmus had initially announced plans
OL,20,Ffor a stock market debut that valued
OL,21,Fthe company at more than $30bn
OL,22,F(#22.65bn).
OL,23,APub: 09-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG5/18
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
